================================================================================
Third-party attributions — code emitted into generated sketches
================================================================================

The native display and touch paths (framework-avr, framework-esp32) emit C++
adapter code into the sketches this project transpiles. Some of that code is
ported or transcribed from third-party BSD-3-Clause and MIT sources. End users
distributing firmware built from those sketches should retain the attributions
below.

The Adafruit (arduino-cli) path does NOT bundle or emit Adafruit-derived
code — it links the Adafruit libraries directly, and end users retain the
Adafruit library LICENSE/attribution files through normal Arduino library
distribution.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Adafruit_GFX geometry algorithms  (BSD-3-Clause)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Source:     Adafruit_GFX.cpp / Adafruit_GFX.h
  Copyright:  (c) 2013 Adafruit Industries. All rights reserved.
  License:    BSD-3-Clause
  Upstream:   https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit-GFX-Library

  Used by:    packages/ui/src/ui-engine/runtime-header/cuttlefish-gfx.ts
              (the CuttlefishGFX class — geometry/canvas/text base emitted
              only when a native display adapter is active)

  Scope:      The following method implementations are ported from
              Adafruit_GFX.cpp: drawLine (Bresenham), drawCircle
              (midpoint), drawCircleHelper, fillCircleHelper, drawRoundRect,
              fillRoundRect, drawTriangle, fillTriangle, drawChar, and the
              glyph loop in write(). Pixel output is byte-for-byte
              identical to Adafruit_GFX.

